  "question": {
    "text": "A solution containing active cobalt <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>Co</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>27</mn><mn>60</mn></mmultiscripts></math> having an activity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.8</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>μCi</mi></math> and decay constant <math><mi>λ</mi></math> is injected in an animal's body. When&nbsp;<math><mn>1</mn><mi>&nbsp;c</mi><msup><mrow><mn>m</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;blood is drawn from the animal's body after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math> of injection, the activity was found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>dpm</mi></math>(decays per minute), then the total volume of blood in the animal's body is close to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>Ci</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.7</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>dps</mi></math>(decays per second) and at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math>&nbsp;the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.84</mn><mo>]</mo></math>",
